# Cursor Rules — MERN Starter

See `CLAUDE.md` and `AGENTS.md` for the full project conventions. Cursor honors `.cursorrules`; this file mirrors the load-bearing subset for quick reference. The authoritative rule files live in `.claude/rules/`.

## Stack

MongoDB + Express + React + Node. Client uses Webpack/React 15 today; modernization to Vite + React 18 + TypeScript happens in prompts 10–13. Server uses Mongoose 4 + Express 4 + Mocha; modernizes to Mongoose 8 + TypeScript + Vitest.

## Load-bearing rules

- **Feature-module isolation** — Client features live in `client/src/features/<name>/`; server modules in `server/src/modules/<name>/`. Cross-feature imports go through `shared/` or each module's `index.js` public API. Never reach into another feature's internals. → `.claude/rules/mern-feature-modules.md`

- **Named exports only** — No `export default` on components, actions, reducers, models, or utilities. → `.claude/rules/mern-no-default-exports.md`

- **Typed Mongoose schemas** — Every schema gets a JSDoc `@typedef` (today) or `InferSchemaType` (post-TS). Type is exported alongside the model. → `.claude/rules/mern-mongoose-typed-schemas.md`

- **Root `.env` only** — Never create `.env` files in subdirectories. All config flows through `process.env` or build-time injection. → `.claude/rules/environment-variables.md`

- **No hardcoded URLs** — All URLs derive from `CLIENT_URL` and `SERVER_URL` env vars. → `.claude/rules/site-url-env-pattern.md`

- **Tab state in URL query params** — Every tabbed interface persists active tab as `?tab=` so links are shareable and refresh-safe. Never use `useState` for tab state. → `.claude/rules/url-tab-state.md`

- **Anti-Codex UI patterns** — No card-lift-on-hover, gradient text, pill buttons, bounce/pulse animations, or `transition: all`. Flat borders, 6px button radius, 8px card radius, 150ms max transitions on `color`/`opacity` only. → `.claude/rules/ui-ux-patterns.md`

- **Destructive git commands require explicit confirmation** — `git stash`, `git reset --hard`, `git clean -f`, `git commit --amend`, `git push --force`, and similar must never run without per-turn user approval. → `.claude/rules/git-destructive-commands.md`

- **Spec-driven development for non-trivial features** — Start with a spec (problem statement, acceptance criteria, edge cases) before implementation. Bug fixes and one-liners skip the full workflow. → `.claude/rules/spec-driven-development.md`

## What this repo does NOT do

No Docker, no SSR, no monorepo tooling, no GraphQL, no tRPC, no Postgres/Redis, no CSS-in-JS, no design system. REST + Sass + hand-written components.
